    "AI Notes": {
      "value": "Italian, London-based 3D/CGI and motion designer and creative director. Co-founder of ffforum (2025-present), a design practice for art and innovation clients; previously Porto Rocha (2023-24), CC Studio (2021-23), Monotype (2020-21). CGI and motion direction for Apple (AirPods), Nike (Shox), Puma (Speedcat), Jamie xx, Boiler Room; tools Cinema 4D and After Effects; featured by Creative Review. His work is motion/video: project films embedded from Vimeo with poster thumbnails as previews, plus render stills. Instagram @vmragona, also Behance and are.na. Work Status: Studio (co-founder ffforum), also takes freelance direction. Jonathan rates him 4 and notes he has worked with Porto Rocha, Colin Doerffler and Apple.",
